From: Cyryl Sochacki <cyrylsochacki@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] udev: ignore single-touch emulation on multi-touch devices

For multi-touch devices the kernel also sends single-touch emulation
events (ABS_X, ABS_Y, BTN_TOUCH) that follow the oldest active contact.
The touch code applied them to slot 0 (BTN_TOUCH even to the current
slot) on top of the MT slot data. When another contact outlives the first
one, the emulation moves to it: slot 0 got that contact's position and a
second touch up ("Cannot report touch up since there are no active
points!"), and the menu saw phantom releases and taps while scrolling.

The MT slots carry the same information, so use only them when the device
has MT slots. Single-touch devices (no ABS_MT_SLOT) are unchanged.

Tested on Allwinner A20 with an FT5x06 touchscreen (which also reports
phantom contacts), KMS + udev, RetroArch 1.20.0.

---
--- a/input/drivers/udev_input.c
+++ b/input/drivers/udev_input.c
@@ -2695,6 +2695,12 @@
                }
                break;
             case ABS_X:
+               /* Multi-touch devices: the kernel also sends single-touch
+                * emulation (ABS_X/ABS_Y/BTN_TOUCH) that follows the oldest
+                * contact, even a phantom one after the real finger lifted.
+                * The MT slots already carry the same data, so skip it. */
+               if (touch->info_slots.enabled && touch->info_slots.range > 1)
+                  break;
                /* TODO - Currently using single-touch events as touch with id 0 */
                RARCH_DDBG("[udev] handle_touch: [0] ST_X to %d\n", event->value);
                touch->staging[0].pos_x = event->value;
@@ -2719,6 +2725,12 @@
                   touch->staging[touch->current_slot].td_pos_x = event->value;
                break;
             case ABS_Y:
+               /* Multi-touch devices: the kernel also sends single-touch
+                * emulation (ABS_X/ABS_Y/BTN_TOUCH) that follows the oldest
+                * contact, even a phantom one after the real finger lifted.
+                * The MT slots already carry the same data, so skip it. */
+               if (touch->info_slots.enabled && touch->info_slots.range > 1)
+                  break;
                /* TODO - Currently using single-touch events as touch with id 0 */
                RARCH_DDBG("[udev] handle_touch: [0] ST_Y to %d\n", event->value);
                touch->staging[0].pos_y = event->value;
@@ -2776,6 +2788,10 @@
       case EV_KEY:
          if (event->code == BTN_TOUCH)
          {
+            /* Multi-touch devices: touch down/up comes from the MT tracking
+             * IDs; BTN_TOUCH is only the single-touch emulation (see ABS_X). */
+            if (touch->info_slots.enabled && touch->info_slots.range > 1)
+               break;
             RARCH_DDBG("[udev] handle_touch: [%d] TOUCH %d\n", touch->current_slot, event->value);
             if (event->value > 0)
                touch->staging[touch->current_slot].change = UDEV_TOUCH_CHANGE_DOWN;
